2    . A
3                . D
4                   . F       
5             . C
6              
7                . E
8    . B
9                   . G

For the plane above, the input will be: 
[
  [2,2], // A
  [2,8], // B
  [5,5], // C
  [6,3], // D
  [6,7], // E
  [7,4], // F
  [7,9]  // G
]
=> closest pair is: [[6,3],[7,4]] or [[7,4],[6,3]]
(both answers are valid)

[
  [2,2], // A
  [2,8], // B
  [5,5], // C
  [6,3], // D
  [6,7], // E
  [7,4], // F
  [7,9]  // G
]
=> closest pair is: [[6,3],[7,4]] or [[7,4],[6,3]]
(both answers are valid)

(
  (2,2), # A
  (2,8), # B
  (5,5), # C
  (6,3), # D
  (6,7), # E
  (7,4), # F
  (7,9)  # G
)
=> closest pair is: ((6,3),(7,4)) or ((7,4),(6,3))
(both answers are valid. You can return a list of tuples too)

